{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"color-camera","name":"Colour-tracking camera","version":"1.1.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","needsApp":"0.13.0","description":"A small camera that finds the biggest patch of one colour (red, green, blue, yellow...) in what it sees and tells a board where it is over I2C, like the Pixy or HuskyLens cameras robots use. A screen on its back shows what it sees. Includes BlobCam.h for sketches.","category":"Sensors","code":"// A colour-tracking camera: it looks at the bench through its \"eye\" camera, finds the pixels of the\n// colour it's tracking, and reports where they are over I2C, like a Pixy or HuskyLens.\n//\n// How it sees: part.camera('eye') gives pictures (80 x 60 RGBA) of the bench from its lens, 15 a\n// second. For each picture: every pixel whose hue is close to the target's (and that is colourful and\n// bright enough to tell) counts as \"found\"; their middle is the target's position.\n//\n// I2C (address 0x54): write [0x00] then read 6 bytes: found (0/1), x (0-255, left to right),\n// y (0-255, top to bottom), width, height (0-255), size (how much of the picture it fills, 0-255).\n// Write [0x10, r, g, b] to track another colour.\nbench.device('blobcam', (part) => {\n  const eye = part.camera('eye');\n  const view = part.screen('view');\n  const addr = Number(part.params.addr ?? 0x54);\n  let powered = false, pointer = 0, frames = 0, lastFrame = -1;\n  let target = hsv(255, 0, 0); // red to start with\n  const found = { yes: 0, x: 128, y: 128, w: 0, h: 0, size: 0 };\n\n  function hsv(r, g, b) {\n    const mx = Math.max(r, g, b), mn = Math.min(r, g, b), d = mx - mn;\n    let h = 0;\n    if (d) h = mx === r ? ((g - b) / d) % 6 : mx === g ? (b - r) / d + 2 : (r - g) / d + 4;\n    return { h: (h * 60 + 360) % 360, s: mx ? d / mx : 0, v: mx / 255 };\n  }\n  const hueGap = (a, b) => Math.min(Math.abs(a - b), 360 - Math.abs(a - b));\n\n  /** look at a new picture: where is the colour? and draw it on the back screen */\n  function analyse(f) {\n    let n = 0, sx = 0, sy = 0, x0 = f.width, y0 = f.height, x1 = -1, y1 = -1;\n    const hit = new Uint8Array(f.width * f.height);\n    for (let y = 0; y < f.height; y++)\n      for (let x = 0; x < f.width; x++) {\n        const i = (y * f.width + x) * 4;\n        const c = hsv(f.data[i], f.data[i + 1], f.data[i + 2]);\n        if (c.s > 0.45 && c.v > 0.2 && hueGap(c.h, target.h) < 22) {\n          hit[y * f.width + x] = 1;\n          n++; sx += x; sy += y;\n          if (x < x0) x0 = x; if (x > x1) x1 = x; if (y < y0) y0 = y; if (y > y1) y1 = y;\n        }\n      }\n    const min = Math.max(3, (f.width * f.height) / 1500); // a few pixels of noise isn't a find\n    found.yes = n >= min ? 1 : 0;\n    if (found.yes) {\n      found.x = Math.round(((sx / n) / (f.width - 1)) * 255);\n      found.y = Math.round(((sy / n) / (f.height - 1)) * 255);\n      found.w = Math.round(((x1 - x0 + 1) / f.width) * 255);\n      found.h = Math.round(((y1 - y0 + 1) / f.height) * 255);\n      found.size = Math.min(255, Math.round((n / (f.width * f.height)) * 255 * 4));\n    } else found.size = 0;\n    // the back screen: what it sees (32 x 24), what it found brighter, and a cross on the target\n    const cx = found.yes ? Math.round((found.x / 255) * (view.cols - 1)) : -1, cy = found.yes ? Math.round((found.y / 255) * (view.rows - 1)) : -1;\n    for (let sy2 = 0; sy2 < view.rows; sy2++)\n      for (let sx2 = 0; sx2 < view.cols; sx2++) {\n        const px = Math.floor(((sx2 + 0.5) / view.cols) * f.width), py = Math.floor(((sy2 + 0.5) / view.rows) * f.height);\n        const [r, g, b] = f.get(px, py);\n        const isHit = hit[py * f.width + px];\n        const k = isHit ? 1 : 0.55;\n        let col = `rgb(${Math.round(r * k)},${Math.round(g * k)},${Math.round(b * k)})`;\n        if ((sx2 === cx && Math.abs(sy2 - cy) <= 2) || (sy2 === cy && Math.abs(sx2 - cx) <= 2)) col = '#ffffff';\n        view.set(sx2, sy2, col);\n      }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? addr : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\n        pointer = bytes[0];\n        if (bytes[0] === 0x10 && bytes.length >= 4) {\n          target = hsv(bytes[1], bytes[2], bytes[3]);\n          part.log(`tracking hue ${Math.round(target.h)}`);\n        }\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        const regs = [found.yes, found.x, found.y, found.w, found.h, found.size];\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[pointer + i] ?? 0);\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const now = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3.0;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        eye.want(powered ? 15 : 0); // pictures only while it has power (15 a second: the most a camera gets)\n        view.light(powered);\n        if (!powered) view.fill(0);\n      }\n      const f = eye.frame;\n      if (powered && f && f.time !== lastFrame) {\n        lastFrame = f.time;\n        frames++;\n        analyse(f);\n      }\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC 3.3-5 V)'];\n      if (!frames) return ['starting its camera...'];\n      return [found.yes ? `sees it at x ${found.x}, y ${found.y} (filling ${Math.round((found.size / 255) * 25)}% of the view)` : 'nothing of that colour in view', `${frames} pictures`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"BlobCam.h":{"classes":["BlobCam"],"code":"// BlobCam for sketches: talks to the colour-tracking camera over I2C (Wire).\n//   BlobCam cam;              (or BlobCam cam(0x55); for the other address)\n//   cam.begin();\n//   cam.setColor(255, 0, 0);  the colour to track (red)\n//   if (cam.read() && cam.found) { cam.x, cam.y (0-255), cam.width, cam.height, cam.size }\nclass BlobCam {\n  constructor(addr = 0x54) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    this.found = false;\n    this.x = 128;\n    this.y = 128;\n    this.width = 0;\n    this.height = 0;\n    this.size = 0;\n  }\n  begin() {\n    Wire.begin();\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; // true if the camera answered\n  }\n  setColor(r, g, b) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    Wire.write(0x10);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    Wire.write(g);\n    Wire.write(b);\n    return Wire.endTransmission() === 0;\n  }\n  /** ask what it sees now; false if the camera didn't answer */\n  read() {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    Wire.write(0x00);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return false;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, 6) !== 6) return false;\n    this.found = Wire.read() === 1;\n    this.x = Wire.read();\n    this.y = Wire.read();\n    this.width = Wire.read();\n    this.height = Wire.read();\n    this.size = Wire.read();\n    return true;\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"blobcam","name":"Colour-tracking camera","description":"Looks along its lens (the +x side). VCC 3.3-5 V, GND, SDA, SCL; I2C address 0x54. In a sketch: #include <BlobCam.h>, BlobCam cam; cam.begin(); cam.setColor(255, 0, 0); then if (cam.read() && cam.found) use cam.x (0 = left edge, 255 = right), cam.y, cam.size. The screen on its back shows its view, with a cross on what it found.","swatch":"#2a6fd6","mass":8,"params":[{"key":"addr","label":"I2C address","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"84","label":"0x54"},{"value":"85","label":"0x55"}]}],"defaults":{"addr":"84"},"shape":[{"box":[1,2.6,3],"at":[0,1.3,0],"color":"#2a6fd6"},{"cyl":[0.55,0.5],"at":[0.75,1.6,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#151618"},{"cyl":[0.35,0.52],"at":[0.77,1.6,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#3a4a7a","collide":false},{"screen":{"id":"view","size":[2.6,1.95],"px":[32,24],"dots":false,"bg":"#000000","off":"#000000"},"at":[-0.505,1.4,0],"rot":[90,0,90]},{"camera":{"id":"eye","px":[80,60],"fov":55,"look":[1,0,0],"range":600},"at":[1.05,1.6,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","SDA","SCL"],"at":[-0.75,0,-0.381],"dir":"z","header":false,"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","SDA":"i2c","SCL":"i2c"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"blobcam"}],"examples":[{"name":"Rover chases a red ball","description":"A rover with the camera on its nose turns towards a red ball, drives to it and stops in front of it. Move the ball (drag it while running) and it follows.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Rover chases a red ball","libraries":[{"id":"color-camera","name":"Colour-tracking camera","version":"1.0.0"}],"parts":[{"uid":"chassis","type":"plate","name":"Chassis","params":{"w":12,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,4.4,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motorR","type":"motor-tt","name":"Right motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.15,3.55],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"motorL","type":"motor-tt","name":"Left motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[3.2,-0.15,-3.55],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelR","type":"wheel","name":"Right wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorR","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,1,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelL","type":"wheel","name":"Left wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorL","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"caster","type":"caster","name":"Caster","params":{"r":1.57},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.6,-0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-18650","name":"Batteries (2x 18650, 7.4 V)","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-2.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"brain","type":"maker-board","name":"Brain","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[2.6,0.15,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071]},{"uid":"driver","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"battery","body":"body"},"pos":[0,2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"camera","type":"color-camera/blobcam","name":"Camera","params":{"addr":"84"},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[5.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"ball","type":"ball","name":"Red ball","params":{"r":3,"material":"plastic","color":"#e02828"},"parent":null,"pos":[55,0,-28],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"VM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND2"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN1"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN2"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN1"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN2"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M-"},"color":"#ff9d3a"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M-"},"color":"#ff9d3a"},{"id":"c1","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"c2","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"c3","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"c4","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"brain":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Rover chases a red ball: the colour-tracking camera on its nose says where red is in its view;\n// the rover turns towards it, drives up to it and stops when it fills the view. Drag the ball\n// somewhere else while it runs and it goes after it. Nothing red in view: it turns on the spot to look.\n#include <BlobCam.h>\n\n#define AIN1 2    // right motor, through the DRV8833\n#define AIN2 3\n#define BIN1 5    // left motor\n#define BIN2 6\n\nBlobCam cam;\n\nvoid motor(int in1, int in2, int speed) {\n  speed = constrain(speed, -255, 255);\n  if (speed >= 0) { analogWrite(in1, speed); analogWrite(in2, 0); }\n  else            { analogWrite(in1, 0);     analogWrite(in2, -speed); }\n}\n\nvoid drive(int left, int right) {   // -255 .. 255\n  motor(BIN1, BIN2, left);\n  motor(AIN2, AIN1, right);         // the right motor faces the other way\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!cam.begin()) Serial.println(\"no camera on I2C: check its wires\");\n  cam.setColor(255, 0, 0);          // look for red\n  Serial.println(\"looking for red\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (cam.read() && cam.found) {\n    int err = cam.x - 128;              // how far from the middle (left: negative)\n    if (cam.size > 140) {\n      drive(0, 0);                      // it fills the view: we are there\n      Serial.println(\"got it!\");\n    } else if (abs(err) > 40) {\n      // off to one side: turn on the spot towards it, slower as it nears the middle\n      // (turning fast overshoots: the camera only looks 15 times a second)\n      int t = constrain(err / 2, -75, 75);\n      if (t > 0 && t < 55) t = 55;      // below this the gearbox won't turn\n      if (t < 0 && t > -55) t = -55;\n      drive(t, -t);\n    } else {\n      int speed = 160 - cam.size * 3 / 4; // slower as it gets closer (bigger in the view)\n      if (speed < 70) speed = 70;\n      drive(speed + err / 2, speed - err / 2); // roughly ahead: drive, steering a little\n    }\n  } else {\n    drive(60, -60);                     // nothing red in view: turn slowly and look\n  }\n  delay(30);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Drone follows a red ball","description":"A quadcopter with an ESP32-S3 flight controller: an MPU-6050 keeps it level, a sonar underneath holds its height, and the camera on its nose finds the ball. It takes off, turns to the ball and flies to 50 cm from it. Pick the ball up and move it while it runs (or carry it with WASD) and it follows.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Drone follows a red ball","parts":[{"uid":"frame","type":"plate","name":"Frame","params":{"w":12,"h":0.4,"d":12,"material":"plastic","color":"#3a3d44"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,4.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"arm1","type":"plate","name":"Arm (FR-BL)","params":{"w":28,"h":0.4,"d":2.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.2,0],"rot":[0,0.382683,0,0.92388]},{"uid":"arm2","type":"plate","name":"Arm (FL-BR)","params":{"w":28,"h":0.4,"d":2.5,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.2,0],"rot":[0,-0.382683,0,0.92388]},{"uid":"leg1","type":"rod","name":"Leg 1","params":{"r":0.4,"len":4,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[5,-0.2,5],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"leg2","type":"rod","name":"Leg 2","params":{"r":0.4,"len":4,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[5,-0.2,-5],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"leg3","type":"rod","name":"Leg 3","params":{"r":0.4,"len":4,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-5,-0.2,5],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"leg4","type":"rod","name":"Leg 4","params":{"r":0.4,"len":4,"material":"plastic","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-5,-0.2,-5],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"motorFR","type":"brushless-prop","name":"Motor FR (CCW)","params":{"kv":2300,"prop":5,"pitch":4.3,"spin":"ccw","color":"#d9dce1"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[8.5,0.6000000000000001,8.5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"escFR","type":"esc","name":"ESC FR","params":{"amps":"30"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[4.42,0.6000000000000001,4.42],"rot":[0,0.382683,0,0.92388]},{"uid":"motorFL","type":"brushless-prop","name":"Motor FL (CW)","params":{"kv":2300,"prop":5,"pitch":4.3,"spin":"cw","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[8.5,0.6000000000000001,-8.5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"escFL","type":"esc","name":"ESC FL","params":{"amps":"30"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[4.42,0.6000000000000001,-4.42],"rot":[0,0.92388,0,0.382683]},{"uid":"motorBR","type":"brushless-prop","name":"Motor BR (CW)","params":{"kv":2300,"prop":5,"pitch":4.3,"spin":"cw","color":"#2b2d33"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-8.5,0.6000000000000001,8.5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"escBR","type":"esc","name":"ESC BR","params":{"amps":"30"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.42,0.6000000000000001,4.42],"rot":[0,-0.382683,0,0.92388]},{"uid":"motorBL","type":"brushless-prop","name":"Motor BL (CCW)","params":{"kv":2300,"prop":5,"pitch":4.3,"spin":"ccw","color":"#d9dce1"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-8.5,0.6000000000000001,-8.5],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"escBL","type":"esc","name":"ESC BL","params":{"amps":"30"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.42,0.6000000000000001,-4.42],"rot":[0,0.92388,0,-0.382683]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-lipo","name":"LiPo 4S 1300 mAh","params":{"cells":"4","mAh":1300,"charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.2,0],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"fc","type":"esp32s3-board","name":"Flight controller (ESP32-S3)","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.6000000000000001,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"imu","type":"mpu6050","name":"MPU-6050","params":{"addr":"104"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[-3.6,0.2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"sonar","type":"hcsr04","name":"Height sonar (HC-SR04)","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.2,3.9],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"camera","type":"color-camera/blobcam","name":"Camera","params":{"addr":"84"},"parent":{"uid":"frame","body":"body"},"pos":[6,0.2,0],"rot":[0,0,-0.258819,0.965926]},{"uid":"ball","type":"ball","name":"Red ball","params":{"r":4,"material":"foam","color":"#e02828"},"parent":null,"pos":[95,0,30],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"BAT+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"BAT+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"BAT+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"BAT+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"BAT-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"BAT-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"BAT-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"BAT-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"fc","pin":"5V"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"fc","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"sonar","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"sonar","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO15"},"b":{"uid":"sonar","pin":"TRIG"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w14","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO16"},"b":{"uid":"sonar","pin":"ECHO"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w15","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w16","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w17","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO8"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w18","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO9"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#9b59b6"},{"id":"w19","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w20","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w21","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO8"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w22","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO9"},"b":{"uid":"camera","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#9b59b6"},{"id":"w23","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO4"},"b":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w24","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO5"},"b":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w25","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO6"},"b":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w26","a":{"uid":"fc","pin":"IO7"},"b":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w27","a":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"A"},"b":{"uid":"motorFR","pin":"B"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w28","a":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"B"},"b":{"uid":"motorFR","pin":"A"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w29","a":{"uid":"escFR","pin":"C"},"b":{"uid":"motorFR","pin":"C"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w30","a":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"A"},"b":{"uid":"motorFL","pin":"A"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w31","a":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"B"},"b":{"uid":"motorFL","pin":"B"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w32","a":{"uid":"escFL","pin":"C"},"b":{"uid":"motorFL","pin":"C"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w33","a":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"A"},"b":{"uid":"motorBR","pin":"A"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w34","a":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"B"},"b":{"uid":"motorBR","pin":"B"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w35","a":{"uid":"escBR","pin":"C"},"b":{"uid":"motorBR","pin":"C"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w36","a":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"A"},"b":{"uid":"motorBL","pin":"B"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w37","a":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"B"},"b":{"uid":"motorBL","pin":"A"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w38","a":{"uid":"escBL","pin":"C"},"b":{"uid":"motorBL","pin":"C"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"fc":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Drone follows a red ball. A quadcopter (four 5 inch props on 2300 KV motors, a 4S LiPo) with an\n// ESP32-S3 as its flight controller:\n//   - the MPU-6050 feels how it leans and turns: it keeps it level (and turns it) by speeding up\n//     some motors and slowing others,\n//   - the HC-SR04 underneath measures its height,\n//   - the colour-tracking camera on its nose (tilted 30 degrees down) finds the ball: it turns to\n//     face it, flies to 50 cm from it, and stays 40 cm higher than it.\n// Press Run: the ESCs arm, it takes off, finds the ball and flies to it. Pick the ball up and move\n// it while it runs (or carry it with WASD), lift it slowly: it follows, up too. No ball in view: it\n// turns on the spot to look (lifted out of view: it climbs to look first).\n// Serial (115200) prints what it's doing; press Plot to see the height and distance.\n//\n// Motors, seen from above (nose = +x, where the camera looks):\n//     FL (CW)   FR (CCW)        CW = clockwise props on straight-wired motors,\n//          \\ /                  CCW = counter-clockwise props on motors with two wires swapped:\n//          / \\                  diagonal pairs turn the same way, so their twists cancel.\n//     BL (CCW)  BR (CW)\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <ESP32Servo.h>\n#include <BlobCam.h>\n\n#define PIN_FR 4      // each ESC's signal wire\n#define PIN_FL 5\n#define PIN_BR 6\n#define PIN_BL 7\n#define TRIG 15       // HC-SR04 (looking down)\n#define ECHO 16\n#define MPU 0x68      // MPU-6050 on I2C (with the camera at 0x54)\n\nconst float HOVER_CM = 40;    // height to hold (sonar reading)\nconst float FOLLOW_CM = 50;   // how far from the ball to stay\nconst float CAM_TILT = 30;    // the camera looks this many degrees down\nconst float CAM_UP = 2.5;     // the camera is this much above the sonar\nconst float BALL_R = 4;       // the ball's radius (its middle is this high)\nconst float VFOV = 55;        // the camera's view, top to bottom (degrees); it is 80 x 60 pixels\nconst float DRAG = 0.25;      // the air slows this drone by 25 % of its speed each second\n\nServo escFR, escFL, escBR, escBL;\nBlobCam cam;\n\n// what it knows\nfloat roll = 0, pitch = 0;        // degrees: roll + = right side down, pitch + = nose down\nfloat gxBias = 0, gyBias = 0, gzBias = 0;\nfloat gx = 0, gy = 0, gz = 0;     // turning, degrees a second (after the bias)\nfloat ax = 0, ay = 0, az = 1;     // acceleration, g\nfloat alt = 0, altV = 0;          // height (cm) and how fast it changes (cm/s), from the sonar\nfloat vFwd = 0, vRight = 0;       // how fast it's moving (cm/s), forward and to the right\nfloat ballDist = -1, ballSide = 0, ballHigh = 0;   // where the ball is: cm away, degrees right, cm up\nbool ballSeen = false, sizeBased = false, lostUp = false;\nint lastY = 128;\nfloat dSize = 0, dFloor = 0;      // (the two ways of telling how far it is)\nunsigned long seenAt = 0, lastSonar = 0, lastCam = 0, lastPrint = 0, lastUs = 0, startMs = 0;\n\n// what it's doing\nfloat altTarget = 0;\nfloat iAlt = 0, iRollRate = 0, iPitchRate = 0, iDrift = 0;\nint thrust = 1000;\nint state = 0;   // 0 arming, 1 flying, 2 crashed (motors off)\n\nint16_t rd16() {\n  int v = Wire.read() << 8;\n  v = v | Wire.read();\n  if (v > 32767) v = v - 65536;\n  return v;\n}\n\nvoid mpuWrite(int reg, int val) {\n  Wire.beginTransmission(MPU);\n  Wire.write(reg);\n  Wire.write(val);\n  Wire.endTransmission();\n}\n\nbool readImu() {\n  Wire.beginTransmission(MPU);\n  Wire.write(0x3B);                       // from ACCEL_XOUT_H: accel x y z, temperature, gyro x y z\n  if (Wire.endTransmission() != 0) return false;\n  if (Wire.requestFrom(MPU, 14) != 14) return false;\n  ax = rd16() / 8192.0;                   // +-4 g range\n  ay = rd16() / 8192.0;\n  az = rd16() / 8192.0;\n  rd16();                                 // (temperature)\n  gx = rd16() / 65.5 - gxBias;            // +-500 deg/s range\n  gy = rd16() / 65.5 - gyBias;\n  gz = rd16() / 65.5 - gzBias;\n  return true;\n}\n\nvoid motors(int fr, int fl, int br, int bl) {\n  escFR.writeMicroseconds(constrain(fr, 1000, 2000));\n  escFL.writeMicroseconds(constrain(fl, 1000, 2000));\n  escBR.writeMicroseconds(constrain(br, 1000, 2000));\n  escBL.writeMicroseconds(constrain(bl, 1000, 2000));\n}\n\nvoid readSonar(float dt) {\n  digitalWrite(TRIG, HIGH);\n  delayMicroseconds(10);\n  digitalWrite(TRIG, LOW);\n  long us = pulseIn(ECHO, HIGH, 30000);\n  if (us <= 0 || us > 25000) return;     // no echo\n  // straight down only when level: tilted, the beam is longer than the height\n  float h = us / 58.0 * cos(roll * DEG_TO_RAD) * cos(pitch * DEG_TO_RAD);\n  float v = (h - alt) / dt;\n  altV = 0.6 * altV + 0.4 * v;\n  alt = h;\n}\n\nvoid readCamera(float dt) {\n  if (!cam.read()) return;\n  if (!cam.found) {\n    if (ballSeen && millis() - seenAt > 600) {\n      ballSeen = false;\n      lostUp = lastY < 80;                // it went out of the top of the picture: it was lifted\n      if (lostUp) Serial.println(\"lost the ball upwards: climbing to look for it\");\n      else Serial.println(\"lost the ball: turning to look for it\");\n    }\n    return;\n  }\n  // where it is: the picture's x and y are angles from the middle of the view\n  float tv = tan(VFOV / 2 * DEG_TO_RAD);\n  float th = tv * 80 / 60;\n  float side = atan((cam.x / 255.0 - 0.5) * 2 * th) * RAD_TO_DEG;      // + = to the right\n  float down = CAM_TILT + pitch + atan((cam.y / 255.0 - 0.5) * 2 * tv) * RAD_TO_DEG;   // below level\n  // how far: from how wide it looks (straight-line distance, at any height; its width, because\n  // the shaded underside doesn't look red, so its height comes out short), or, when the edge of\n  // the picture cuts it off, from how far down it looks (as if it's on the floor)\n  float wide = 2 * atan(cam.width / 255.0 * th) * RAD_TO_DEG;     // degrees, side to side\n  bool whole = cam.y - cam.height / 2 > 4 && cam.y + cam.height / 2 < 251 && cam.x - cam.width / 2 > 4 && cam.x + cam.width / 2 < 251;\n  sizeBased = whole && wide > 1;\n  float slant = sizeBased ? BALL_R / sin(wide / 2 * DEG_TO_RAD) : 0;\n  dSize = slant * cos(down * DEG_TO_RAD);                         // (along the floor)\n  dFloor = down > 3 ? (alt + CAM_UP - BALL_R) / tan(down * DEG_TO_RAD) : 300;\n  float d = constrain(sizeBased ? dSize : dFloor, 5, 300);\n  // and how high it is (the floor = 0)\n  float h = sizeBased ? alt + CAM_UP - slant * sin(down * DEG_TO_RAD) : BALL_R;\n  if (!ballSeen) {\n    Serial.print(\"ball seen: \");\n    Serial.print(d, 0);\n    Serial.print(\" cm away, \");\n    Serial.print(side, 0);\n    Serial.print(\" degrees right, \");\n    Serial.print(h, 0);\n    Serial.println(\" cm up\");\n    ballHigh = h;\n  }\n  ballDist = ballSeen ? 0.6 * ballDist + 0.4 * d : d;\n  ballHigh = 0.8 * ballHigh + 0.2 * h;\n  ballSide = side;\n  lastY = cam.y;\n  ballSeen = true;\n  seenAt = millis();\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(TRIG, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(ECHO, INPUT);\n  escFR.setPeriodHertz(400);              // ESCs take fast updates (servos want 50)\n  escFL.setPeriodHertz(400);\n  escBR.setPeriodHertz(400);\n  escBL.setPeriodHertz(400);\n  escFR.attach(PIN_FR, 1000, 2000);\n  escFL.attach(PIN_FL, 1000, 2000);\n  escBR.attach(PIN_BR, 1000, 2000);\n  escBL.attach(PIN_BL, 1000, 2000);\n  motors(1000, 1000, 1000, 1000);         // a low signal arms the ESCs\n\n  Wire.begin();\n  mpuWrite(0x6B, 0x00);                   // wake the MPU-6050\n  mpuWrite(0x1B, 0x08);                   // gyro +-500 deg/s\n  mpuWrite(0x1C, 0x08);                   // accel +-4 g\n  mpuWrite(0x1A, 0x03);                   // its low-pass filter (44 Hz)\n  if (!readImu()) Serial.println(\"no MPU-6050 on I2C: check its wires\");\n  if (!cam.begin()) Serial.println(\"no camera on I2C: check its wires\");\n  cam.setColor(255, 0, 0);                // look for red\n\n  // the gyro reads a little even when still: measure that while it sits on the ground\n  Serial.println(\"keep still: measuring the gyro\");\n  float sx = 0, sy = 0, sz = 0;\n  for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n    readImu();\n    sx += gx; sy += gy; sz += gz;\n  }\n  gxBias = sx / 100; gyBias = sy / 100; gzBias = sz / 100;\n  roll = atan2(ay, az) * RAD_TO_DEG;\n  pitch = atan2(-ax, az) * RAD_TO_DEG;\n  readSonar(0.05);\n  altTarget = alt;\n  delay(1500);                            // (the ESCs arm)\n  Serial.println(\"armed: taking off\");\n  state = 1;\n  startMs = millis();\n  lastUs = micros();\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  float dt = (micros() - lastUs) / 1000000.0;\n  lastUs = micros();\n  dt = constrain(dt, 0.001, 0.05);\n  readImu();\n\n  // how it leans: the gyro (fast, but adds up small errors) nudged very gently by gravity. Only\n  // gently: a flying drone falls with gravity, so its accelerometer can't feel which way is down\n  // (it reads level even while it leans to fly along); trusted more, it would let the drone tip.\n  roll = 0.999 * (roll + gx * dt) + 0.001 * atan2(ay, az) * RAD_TO_DEG;\n  pitch = 0.999 * (pitch + gy * dt) + 0.001 * atan2(-ax, az) * RAD_TO_DEG;\n  // how fast it moves: what the accelerometer does feel sideways in flight is the air pushing\n  // back, which grows with speed (the same trick real flight controllers use, \"rotor drag\")\n  if (alt > 10) {\n    vFwd = 0.9 * vFwd + 0.1 * (-ax * 981 / DRAG);\n    vRight = 0.9 * vRight + 0.1 * (ay * 981 / DRAG);\n  }\n\n  if (millis() - lastSonar >= 50) {       // the sonar 20 times a second\n    float sdt = (millis() - lastSonar) / 1000.0;\n    lastSonar = millis();\n    readSonar(sdt);\n  }\n  if (millis() - lastCam >= 66) {         // the camera has a new picture 15 times a second\n    float cdt = (millis() - lastCam) / 1000.0;\n    lastCam = millis();\n    readCamera(cdt);\n  }\n\n  if (state == 1 && (abs(roll) > 60 || abs(pitch) > 60)) {\n    state = 2;\n    Serial.println(\"crashed (tipped over): motors off\");\n  }\n  if (state != 1) {\n    motors(1000, 1000, 1000, 1000);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // 1. height: climb gently to HOVER_CM above the ball (40 cm: the ball on the floor), then hold it\n  float altWant = HOVER_CM;\n  if (ballSeen) altWant = constrain(ballHigh + HOVER_CM - BALL_R, 25, 150);\n  else if (lostUp && millis() - seenAt < 6000) altWant = 150;    // (up to look; then back down)\n  if (altTarget < altWant) altTarget = min(altWant, altTarget + 25 * dt);\n  else altTarget = max(altWant, altTarget - 25 * dt);\n  float altErr = altTarget - alt;\n  iAlt = constrain(iAlt + 0.5 * altErr * dt, -150, 250);\n  thrust = 1480 + 1.2 * altErr - 0.9 * altV + iAlt;\n\n  // 2. where to go: face the ball, and fly forward (far) or back (too close); sideways, stay put\n  float vWant = 0, yawRateWant = 0;\n  if (ballSeen && alt > 15) {\n    yawRateWant = constrain(-2.0 * ballSide, -60, 60);\n    if (abs(ballSide) < 25) vWant = constrain(0.8 * (ballDist - FOLLOW_CM), -40, 60);   // (facing it)\n  } else if (alt > 25 && !(lostUp && millis() - seenAt < 6000)) {\n    yawRateWant = 30;                     // turn to the left, looking for it\n  }\n  // lean to speed up or slow down: a 1 degree lean pushes it along at about 17 cm/s each second\n  float pitchWant = constrain(0.09 * (vWant - vFwd), -10, 10);\n  iDrift = constrain(iDrift + 0.02 * vRight * dt, -3, 3);   // (a small lean that's always needed)\n  float rollWant = constrain(-0.09 * vRight - iDrift, -10, 10);\n\n  // 3. lean: how fast to tip towards the lean it wants, then the motors to turn it that fast\n  float rollRateWant = 3.0 * (rollWant - roll);\n  float pitchRateWant = 3.0 * (pitchWant - pitch);\n  float eR = rollRateWant - gx, eP = pitchRateWant - gy;\n  iRollRate = constrain(iRollRate + 0.3 * eR * dt, -40, 40);\n  iPitchRate = constrain(iPitchRate + 0.3 * eP * dt, -40, 40);\n  float uRoll = constrain(0.12 * eR + iRollRate, -150, 150);\n  float uPitch = constrain(0.12 * eP + iPitchRate, -150, 150);\n  float uYaw = constrain(1.2 * (yawRateWant - gz), -150, 150);\n\n  // 4. mix: roll right-down = lift the left; nose down = lift the back; turn left = speed up the\n  //    clockwise props (their motors twist the frame the other way)\n  if (alt < 4 && altTarget < 6) { uRoll = 0; uPitch = 0; uYaw = 0; }   // (still on the ground)\n  motors(thrust - uRoll - uPitch - uYaw,    // FR (CCW)\n         thrust + uRoll - uPitch + uYaw,    // FL (CW)\n         thrust - uRoll + uPitch + uYaw,    // BR (CW)\n         thrust + uRoll + uPitch - uYaw);   // BL (CCW)\n\n  if (millis() - lastPrint >= 200) {\n    lastPrint = millis();\n    Serial.print(\"height:\");\n    Serial.print(alt, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" ball:\");\n    Serial.print(ballSeen ? ballDist : 0, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" side:\");\n    Serial.print(ballSeen ? ballSide : 0, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" ballUp:\");\n    Serial.print(ballSeen ? ballHigh : 0, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" bySize:\");\n    Serial.print(dSize, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" byFloor:\");\n    Serial.print(dFloor, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" speed:\");\n    Serial.print(vFwd, 0);\n    Serial.print(\" drift:\");\n    Serial.print(vRight, 0);\n    Serial.print(\" turn:\");\n    Serial.print(gz, 0);\n    Serial.print(\" pitch:\");\n    Serial.print(pitch, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" roll:\");\n    Serial.print(roll, 1);\n    Serial.print(\" thrust:\");\n    Serial.println(thrust - 1000);\n  }\n}\n"}},"boards":[],"libraries":[{"id":"color-camera","name":"Colour-tracking camera","version":"1.1.0"}]}}]}